# Fast seconds: the oscillator can X1 runs at 3 MHz, though marked 1 MHz. The prescaler U1 divides by ten as it should, but from 3 MHz: the hundredths tick three times too fast, so the display reads about 3.00 after one second and rolls over from 9.99 every 3.3 s.
machine stopwatch
title "Fast seconds"
brief "Press START: the seconds run far too fast. After one second the display already reads about 3.00."
fault clock X1 3MHz
